  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A return point has collection crates and space for guests to pause without blocking the serving area.\", \"decision\": \"How should a return point collect used cups?\", \"goal\": \"Make cup lending and return convenient while keeping the available stock and volunteer work understandable.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood café wants to lend reusable cups at community gatherings and recover them afterward. It has a modest cup stock, washable collection crates, a simple lending record, and volunteers who can share short shifts. The plan concerns a small pilot with no deposit or sales system. Different decisions address separate moments in lending, return, and review.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nA volunteer accepts used cups and places them in collection crates as guests arrive. Each returned cup receives an immediate intake check.\nGuests leave used cups on a return ledge, and a volunteer moves them into collection crates in small batches. The ledge separates guest handover from crate handling.\nGuests place used cups directly in collection crates while a volunteer checks the crates at intervals. Return remains quick even when the volunteer is briefly occupied."
    }
